  // folder, `SPC p P` shows the projects. Keys bound here with
  // `vimCommand` come before Vim's own (`-` is no motion any more; remove
  // the binding in keymap.json to have it back). In a listing, Dired's keys (from
  // the Word-like keymap) come before Vim's, except those Vim needs for
  // moving and searching: `n`, `p`, `w` and Backspace. Doom's keys
  // (evil-collection and dirvish, T2.7e.18, the table in
